1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,969
The Volk'ar: an alien hunter, cloaked and invisible, stalking the jungle.

2
00:00:04,189 --> 00:00:05,491
Here's how she plays.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:10,467
Add the two Track cards to your Action Tableau, and put the Attack Resolution card

4
00:00:10,467 --> 00:00:11,889
and tokens beside the board.

5
00:00:12,109 --> 00:00:14,861
Shuffle the Movement deck and deal one card face down.

6
00:00:15,081 --> 00:00:18,324
Her meeple doesn't go on the board. It sits on the Finale card.

7
00:00:18,544 --> 00:00:20,714
One Origin marker goes where she'd start;

8
00:00:20,714 --> 00:00:22,725
the other goes on that face-down card.

9
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:26,728
She has no Movement Value. For most of the game she's Concealed:

10
00:00:26,728 --> 00:00:28,824
always on the board somewhere, but hidden.

11
00:00:29,044 --> 00:00:33,193
If she's Concealed at the start of the Killer phase, resolve the upper Killer Action

12
00:00:33,193 --> 00:00:35,465
on the Finale card. If Visible, the lower one.

13
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,625
Her route is a hidden Path of Movement cards.

14
00:00:38,845 --> 00:00:43,475
An open eye icon adds a card face up. A crossed-out eye adds one face down.

15
00:00:43,695 --> 00:00:47,849
If she was Visible, she vanishes again: the Origin markers go on the new card and

16
00:00:47,849 --> 00:00:48,772
her current space.

17
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:53,776
She breaks cover when you resolve the Reveal icon, when a sixth Movement card joins

18
00:00:53,776 --> 00:00:56,341
the Path, or when an attack on her would do damage.

19
00:00:56,561 --> 00:01:00,693
Place her on the Origin space, then play out each card in order, moving her, and

20
00:01:00,693 --> 00:01:03,431
attacking wherever a card shows a Killer Action line.

21
00:01:04,267 --> 00:01:07,176
The Track action card lets you flip Movement cards over.

22
00:01:07,176 --> 00:01:10,709
If every card in the Path is face up, you know exactly where she is.

23
00:01:10,929 --> 00:01:13,788
And you're never allowed to look through the discarded Movement cards.

24
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:16,656
You can attack a space you think she's in.

25
00:01:16,656 --> 00:01:20,573
Place the Attack token, roll, and park the damage on the Attack Resolution card.

26
00:01:20,793 --> 00:01:24,911
Any damage makes her Path resolve. If she ends on your target, the damage lands.

27
00:01:25,131 --> 00:01:29,184
If not, she ambushes you. Take the Ambush Penalty on the last Movement card.

28
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,165
While she's Concealed, anything measured from the Killer uses the Origin space, and

29
00:01:34,165 --> 00:01:36,272
effects that place the Killer are ignored.

30
00:01:36,492 --> 00:01:40,097
Killer Action lines count as a crossed eye, and Victims don't panic.

31
00:01:40,933 --> 00:01:44,150
A few tips. Use Track to flip cards before a blind attack:

32
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:46,203
every face-up card narrows the guess.

33
00:01:46,423 --> 00:01:49,089
Strike while the Path is short, when she can't have gone far.

34
00:01:49,309 --> 00:01:53,139
She's very beatable: about three wins in four on Final Girl Stats.

35
00:01:53,139 --> 00:01:55,517
But Self Destruct is her toughest Finale.

36
00:01:55,737 --> 00:01:57,849
Keep the rule sheet handy, and good hunting.

